<section id="workflows">
<h2>Three Affiliate Visual Workflows</h2>

<h3>Workflow 1: Product Comparison Graphic (10 minutes)</h3>
<p>A side-by-side comparison graphic converts better than a text table — readers process images 60,000 times faster than text. Here is the workflow: create a new design at 1200×628px (blog header size). Use Magic Write to generate three headline options for the graphic. Place the two products side by side with AI-generated or screenshot images (use Background Remover to isolate them). Add key specs as short text callouts. Use your Brand Kit colours for consistency. Add a subtle CTA arrow pointing to your recommended pick. Export as PNG and embed in your review.</p>

<h3>Workflow 2: Pinterest Pin Template (5 minutes per pin)</h3>
<p>Pinterest drives long-tail affiliate traffic for months after publication. Create a template at 1000×1500px. Set your Brand Kit colours and fonts as defaults. Place a vertical image (AI-generated or stock) as the background. Overlay your headline — Magic Write can generate 5–10 headline variations for A/B testing. Add your logo in the bottom right. Save as a template and reuse for every article. Produce 2–3 pin variations per article with different headlines targeting different search intents.</p>

<h3>Workflow 3: CTA Button Design (3 minutes)</h3>
<p>Most affiliate CTAs are text links or unstyled buttons. A visually distinct CTA — custom-branded, with a relevant icon and benefit-driven copy — consistently outperforms generic buttons in click-through tests. Create a new design at 800×200px. Add a rounded rectangle shape in your accent colour. Place your CTA text using Magic Write to generate 3–4 variations (test benefit-driven vs action-driven language). Add a small arrow icon. Export as PNG and use as a linked image in your article. For a practical implementation of how CTA placement affects conversion, see our <a href="/blog/how-to-write-seo-content-with-ai/">guide to SEO content writing</a>.</p>
</section>

